{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Do not fear, for this one as well, etc.</b> One needs to know what is the fear that the midwife promises her she need not fear, and when we say that the pangs of death were upon her, how does she remove the fear from her by saying <b>for this one as well</b>, etc.? Further, one needs to know her intention in saying ״this one as well״?" "<b>Indeed</b>, it may be explained according to the statement of the Sages, of blessed memory (Genesis Rabbah 82:8), that with Binyamin two twins were born along with him, unlike with Yosef, where only one twin was born — end quote. Therefore, ״and it came to pass, when she was in hard labor,״ the midwife said to her, ״Do not fear״ from the fact that you are struggling in childbirth, lest you be in danger — for you have an unusual pregnancy unlike the first one, and that is the meaning of saying <b>for this one as well</b>, in the added plurality that this one is yours as well, as though she said, ״for this one as well is a son to you.״" "<b>Further</b>, it alludes to what is well known (Niddah 31a), that a woman who labors to give birth to a male child is not in danger, while a woman who labors to give birth to a female child is in danger. Therefore she said: for surely this one as well is to you a son, and you will not be in danger."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 35, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:46:12.813311126Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}